From 782c383767fa1a3ba64f479b7eaaa73dc889815d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kgvarunkanth <kgvarunkanth@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:02:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] blueprint: low-memory mode for 8 GB build hosts

BLUEPRINT_COMPACT_ACTIONS=1 renders each module's build actions to
compressed ninja text as soon as they are generated, instead of holding
the parsed form until the whole build file is written; that was most of
soong_build's peak heap. BLUEPRINT_SKIP_MODULE_TYPES drops test and fuzz
module types at parse time, and long ninja arguments are parsed once and
cached. BLUEPRINT_VARIANT_STATS writes variant and heap diagnostics.

Together these fit the LineageOS 20 Soong graph in 6.3 GB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I71389260a421976be46beadc3e3c90980b1f9e45
---
 Android.bp         |   1 +
 compact_actions.go | 218 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 context.go         |  55 +++++++++---
 ninja_defs.go      |  32 ++++++-
